 "details": {
  "title": "Handel – Lascia ch’io pianga, in C",
  "lead": "Handel’s line for the trumpet a whole step under the D of the lead sheet, in C (D for the trumpet), concert C4 to D5, on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement in the same key, an octave above where the baritone sings it. It plays in that guitar track’s time, about 44 to the quarter, slowing at the end of each part. The first part comes twice, as Handel wrote it; the guitar plays the ritornello alone. The lead sheet in D stays as it is.",
  "facts": [
